{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"863315583080595476","content":"A half goblin, half gnome works the forge and anvil. He doesn't talk much, but when he does his voice is screechy and cracked. This is the local weapons and armorer.","created_at":"2021-07-10T07:09:07.180000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T07:09:27.946000Z","id":"863315887359655966","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"863315583080595476","content":"Battle axe: 100 gp.\nBlow gun: 10 gp\nClub: 1 gold.\nCrossbow bolts: 1 gold per.\nHand Crossbow: 750 gp\nDagger: 200 gp\nFlail: 100 gp\nGlaive: 200 gp\nGreat Axe: 300 gp\nGreat Sword: 500 gp\n\n**Greater Sword\nUncommon: 3,000\nTwo-handed, Heavy, Reach 10ft\nRequires at least 16 Strength\n\nEven the strongest of combatants find this oversized blade unwieldy, but damn does it look cool.\n\nThis magical greatsword deals 3d6 slashing damage on hit, that is if you can hit. This sword normally rolls at disadvantage (which may be neutralized by advantage).**\n\nHalberd: 200 gp\nHandaxe: 50 gp\nJavelin: 5 gp per\nLight Hammer: 20 gp\nLong bow: 500 gp\nLong sword: 150 gp\nMace 50 gp\nMaul 50 gp\nMorningstar: 150 gp\nPike: 50gp\nShortbow: 250 gp\nShortsword: 100 gp\nSickle: 10 gp\nSpear: 30 gp\nWar Pick: 20 gp\nWarhammer: 150 gp\nWhip 20 gp:","created_at":"2021-07-10T07:28:48.640000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-17T11:20:07.768000Z","id":"863320842762977290","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"863315583080595476","content":"For Gleaming versions of armor, add 50 gold.\nFor Cast off, add 100\n\nBreastplate: 400 gp\nChainmail: 750 gp\nChain Shirt: 500 gp\nHalf Plate: 750 gp\nHide: 100 gp\nLeather: 100 gp\nPadded: 500 gp\nPlate: 1,500 gp\nRing Mail: 300 \nScale Mail: 500\nSheild: 1,000 gp","created_at":"2021-07-10T07:36:27.050000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-17T11:21:10.980000Z","id":"863322765472956437","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"863315583080595476","content":"You may augment your armor or weapons with the follwing materials. However: adding Strands of the Ley or Staaten Steel adds a further 7,500 gp cost to the item. May not be applied to used item unless you bring in your own materials.\n\nStrands of Ley (The City)- These threads are soaked in the leylines that meet in the City, absorbing the ambient magical energy. Robes weaved and leather armors stitched with these threads are able to once per day absorb one spell equal to or less than half your proficiency bonus. You may as an action, on your next turn, redirect the spell at another target per the spell’s rules. Bows and Crossbows strung with the thread count as a spell focus and deal additional force damage equal to your proficiency bonus.\n\nStaaten Steel (The city)- Weapons forged w/ this material are considered one weight less than normal weapons. Heavy weapons lose the Heavy Property, Non Light weapons gain the light property. Armor forged from this steel are lighter weight, removing any penalty to stealth checks and Heavy armors count as Medium armor and Medium armor count as Light armor","created_at":"2021-07-10T07:38:40.699000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-22T07:20:51.841000Z","id":"863323326037491754","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
